---
/**
 * pages/[...slug].astro
 *
 * Catch-all route for the CMS-authored public pages. Three published sources claim slugs (impl §6.6): the
 * `pages` and `posts` content types (posts under a `/posts/` prefix) and the compositor's `design_page`
 * type. `route-authority.ts` merges them, fails the build on any duplicate slug so a path always has
 * exactly one owner, and — per the content-routing pivot (D4) — resolves each entry to the design template
 * it renders *through*, if it names one. An entry that names no template renders exactly as it did before
 * the compositor existed (D3), which is what keeps designs strictly opt-in.
 *
 * The page is prerendered: getStaticPaths() enumerates both sources at build time over EmDash's HTTP API
 * (src/lib/build/{emdash,design}-api.ts, through a Cloudflare Access service token). Because only
 * published slugs are built, an unknown path matches no route and is served the static 404 from the
 * Cloudflare ASSETS binding — with no D1 or KV lookup. Publishing or editing a page requires a site
 * rebuild (the admin Rebuild button) to regenerate these static pages.
 *
 * Design pages ship ZERO JavaScript: Puck's `Render` is imported from `@puckeditor/core/rsc` and used with
 * no client directive, so it server-renders to plain HTML. The theme's tokens are injected into the head
 * as `--dtk-*` custom properties alongside the component stylesheet. A design page does NOT emit an
 * automatic <h1>{title}</h1> — its headings come from the canvas (§4.5) — while a Portable-Text page still
 * does, preserving the pre-compositor output.
 *
 * As a rest-parameter route this has the lowest routing priority, so explicit files (index.astro,
 * privacy-policy.astro, the /admin and /api trees) always win.
 *
